{"violation_type":{"id":"tx-tac-hrc42-04412-a-interference-with-an-in","jurisdiction":"TX","state":"TX","code_system":"Texas Administrative Code, Title 26, Ch. HRC42","original_code":"HRC42.04412(a) - Interference with an in","title":"HRC42.04412(a) - Interference with an investigation (26 TAC §HRC42.04412(a) - Interference with an in)","short_title":"HRC42.04412(a) - Interference with an investigation","severities":{"high":15},"facility_ids":["tx-hhsc-1215104","tx-hhsc-1389433","tx-hhsc-168375","tx-hhsc-1424708","tx-hhsc-1350058","tx-hhsc-1385266","tx-hhsc-361580","tx-hhsc-1314813","tx-hhsc-1355811","tx-hhsc-1433405","tx-hhsc-104392","tx-hhsc-1331584","tx-hhsc-377980","tx-hhsc-170021","tx-hhsc-1304549"],"first_date":"2021-10-04","last_date":"2023-07-19","typical_finding":"The operation staff interfered with the inspection when staff did not open the door for the inspector to enter the operation until after 8 minutes of knocking,  ringing doorbell and calling the operation's phone number.","finding_variants":[{"text":"The operation staff interfered with the inspection when staff did not open the door for the inspector to enter the operation until after 8 minutes of knocking,  ringing doorbell and calling the operation's phone number.","count":1},{"text":"Throughout the duration of the investigation which began in October 2021, the provider has failed to cooperate with Child Care Regulation Unregulated Operations Inspectors at 16 attempted investigation inspections. Due to the providers lack of cooperation during the investigation, an Access Order was obtained on March 24, 2022, requiring the provider allow inspectors to inspect the home and review records.  Multiple inspections were attempted on six different days, since the access order was issued, with law enforcement support, and the provider is still failing to cooperate with inspectors and continues to deny access to inspectors with confirmed children in care.","count":1},{"text":"During the initial investigati